Build Instructions

1. Install PostgreSQL and pgAdmin4 
     Download and install PostgreSQL and pgAdmin4 from their official websites.

2. Clone the Repository from GitHub:
     git clone https://github.com/eececan/CS319-1-Project.git

3. Open the source code in your preferred IDE

4. Configure Database Settings
     Update the application.properties file to match your existing database configuration, or create a new database with the following properties listed in our application.properties file:
     spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/
     spring.datasource.username=postgres
     spring.datasource.password=password

5. Run the Application Twice
     From the IDE, simply run the application twice to initialize data. The first run will initialize the roles, and the second run will initialize the default users.

6. Configure Mail Services (Optional)
     If you want to change the email address that sends the application/rejection/cancellation mails, you can configure the settings in application.properties file:
     spring.mail.username=<your login user to smtp server>
     spring.mail.password=<your login password to smtp server>

     If not, make sure application.properties looks like this:
     spring.mail.username=dilekyildizbto@gmail.com
     spring.mail.password=qbie hzgf eesz wkfj

 7. Access the Application
     Enter http://localhost:8080/home to your browser after running the application.

